DP  - 2024 Mar 15
TI  - Deep learning-based weed detection in maize fields from multispectral UAV
      imagery: a comparison of convolutional architectures.
PG  - 1821
LID - 10.1000/m5c-1 [doi]
LID - 1821 [pii]
AB  - Site-specific weed management depends on accurate weed maps. We compared three
      convolutional architectures for detecting weeds in maize from multispectral
      unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) imagery acquired at 20 m above ground. The best
      model reached a mean intersection over union of 0.81 across two growing
      seasons. Results indicate that early-season flights give the most useful
      prescription maps.
